 kg</FONT></TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width=590 align=center border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0><tr><td height=12></td></tr></table><TABLE width=590 align=center border=0><TR><TD width=20></TD><TD><b>Explanation： </b>The method of calculating standard body weight by the World Health Organization</TD></TR><TR><TD width=20></TD><TD>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Male：（Height cm－80）×70﹪ <br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;female：（Height cm－70）×60﹪。</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width=590 align=center      border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0><tr><td height=20></td></tr></table><TABLE width=590 align=center border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0><tr><td height=12></td></tr></table><TABLE align=center cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=0      width=600 bgColor=#c0c0c0 border=1><TR><TD align=middle width=124 bgColor=#c0c0c0><B><FONT size=2>property</FONT></B></TD><TD align=middle width=150><B><FONT size=2>Low standard</FONT></B></TD><TD align=middle width=100><B><FONT size=2>    Standard</FONT></B></TD><TD align=middle width=226><B><FONT size=2>Exceed the standard</FONT></B></TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE align=center cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=0 width=600 border=0><TR><TD width=100>&nbsp;<WBR></TD><TD align=middle width=50>|    </TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD>   <TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD></TD></TR><TR><TD width=100>&nbsp;<WBR></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>60%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>70%</FONT></TD>                <TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>80%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>90%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>100%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>110%</FONT></TD>             <TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>120%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>130%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>140%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>150%</FONT></TD></TR>      </TABLE><TABLE align=center cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=0 width=600 border=0><TR><TD width=125 align=center><FONT size=2>③Muscle weight</FONT></TD><TD align=left width=475 colSpan=10 valign=center><img src=Mark.jpg width=MyValue14
 height=15 border=0/>&nbsp;<FONT size=3>MyValue15
Kg</FONT></TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width=590 align=center border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0><tr><td height=12></td></tr></table><TABLE width=590 align=center border=0><TR><TD width=20></TD><TD><b>Explanation： </b>For the average person, muscle accounts for 35% to 45% of their body weight. Being overweight does not mean simply reducing muscle mass; instead, it should involve converting the fat weight in the body into muscle weight. Because the muscle mass increases, the basal metabolic rate rises. Basal metabolic rate refers to the energy that must be consumed to maintain basic bodily functions such as body temperature, respiration and blood circulation. When muscle mass increases, basal metabolism also rises. Even when the body is at rest, it can burn fat and form a body that is less likely to gain weight. Therefore, when the basal metabolism increases, even if the food intake remains the same as before, fat will gradually decrease. So first of all, one should increase the muscle mass in their body and raise the basal metabolic rate in order to achieve the goal of slimming down. Build muscle strength and do more aerobic exercises.</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width=590 align=center border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0><tr><td height=20></td></tr></table><TABLE width=590 align=center border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0><tr><td height=12></td></tr>   </table><TABLE align=center cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=0 width=600 bgColor=#c0c0c0 border=1><TR><TD align=middle width=124 bgColor=#c0c0c0><B><FONT size=2>property</FONT></B></TD><TD align=middle width=150><B><FONT size=2>Low standard   </FONT></B></TD><TD align=middle width=100><B><FONT size=2>Standard</FONT></B></TD><TD align=middle width=226><B><FONT size=2>Exceed the standard</FONT></B></TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE align=center cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=0 width=600 border=0>   <TR><TD width=100>&nbsp;<WBR></TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD>  <TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD><TD align=middle width=50>|</TD></TD></TR><TR><TD width=100>&nbsp;<WBR></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>20%</FONT></TD>   <TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>40%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>60%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>80%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>100%</FONT></TD><TD       align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>120%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>140%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>160%</FONT></TD><TD align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>180%</FONT></TD><TD        align=middle width=50><FONT size=2>200%</FONT></TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE align=center cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=0 width=600 border=0><TR><TD width=125 align=center><FONT size=2>④Body fat content</FONT></TD><TD align=left width=475      colSpan=10 valign=center><img src=Mark.jpg width=MyValue16
